<title>USA: Pegasus to buy five DirecTV providers.</title>
<headline>Pegasus to buy five DirecTV providers.</headline>
<dateline>RADNOR, Pa. 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pegasus Communications Corp said Wednesday it plans to buy five independent DirecTV providers in three states for $37 million.</p>
<p>The company said it will pay $33.9 million in cash plus $3.1 million in deferred payments for the systems, which were not identified. The company said the systems were in rural locations in the Southeast, upper Midwest and Mountain states.</p>
<p>The company said the systems serve 18,200 customers, but the territories include more than 254,000 television households.</p>
</text>
